# Paths an agent session must never read (ADR-20260816-020752, farley).
#
# THE TEST for a line here: DENY WHAT NO VERDICT IS EVER DERIVED FROM. Build output, object stores
# and vendored trees are re-derivable from source, so reading them can only cost tokens -- never
# change a gate result.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and they must stay readable:
#   specs/generated/**                        -- the codegen drift gate's EVIDENCE; denying it makes
#                                                `check-drift` unauditable by the agent that must fix it
#   Cargo.lock                                -- reproducible CI; a lock diff IS a supply-chain review
#   tools/codegen-rs/warning-baseline.json    -- the warning ratchet; a diff here is the record of
#                                                what a change did to the warning surface
#
# The hard blocks below are MIRRORED in .claude/settings.json `permissions.deny`, so a proactive read
# is stopped even by a client that never loads this file. Keep the two lists in step.

# Rust build output (target/, and the codegen's own target/).
target/
**/target/
tools/codegen-rs/out/

# Vendored / installed dependency trees.
**/node_modules/
**/vendor/

# Git internals -- an object store is bytes, never a verdict.
.git/objects/
.git/lfs/

# Compiled and binary artifacts. WASM bundles are build output of crates/web; the source is Rust.
**/*.wasm
**/*.rlib
**/*.rmeta
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.dll
**/*.a
**/*.o
**/*.bin
**/*.zip
**/*.gz
**/*.tar

# Binary documents and images: no verdict is derived from them, and PDFs cannot be read in this
# container at all (docs/claude/sessions.md) -- a read attempt is a pure loss.
**/*.pdf
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.ico
**/*.woff
**/*.woff2

# Structurizr Lite staging (built by `make c4-render`) and agent worktrees.
.structurizr/
.claude/worktrees/
wt*/

# Filtered-gate logs (`make test-quiet` / `make rust-quiet`) -- read the wrapper's summary, and open
# this file deliberately with an offset when a verdict needs its surrounding context.
target/quiet-gate.log

# QMD advisory retrieval cache — derived, never agent context (row RETRIEVAL-QMD-ROWS).
# Deliberately NOT mirrored in settings.json permissions.deny: `RETRIEVAL-QMD-ROWS` (the chain head)
# carries that non-authorization forward, as its predecessors did before it. THE PROVENANCE IS THE
# CHAIN, NOT THE HEAD: the constraint was first recorded on #671 under the now-superseded
# `RETRIEVAL-QMD`; it was NOT recorded on #679, where `RETRIEVAL-QMD-CI` was opened and decided the
# same day (2026-08-24); and it is carried forward again here (#840, 2026-09-01) without being
# re-decided. That distinction is the whole lesson of this comment: an earlier sweep did s/OLD/NEW/
# on the row name and thereby attributed the constraint to a row about wiring a suite into CI --
# the shortest green, and false. The citation rule ships a clause-scoped escape precisely so a
# sentence ABOUT a superseded row can stay accurate, so cite the HEAD for the live constraint and
# name the older rows as history, which is what the sentences above now do.
.qmd/
